    llm_caret_native_entry_closure_bare_builtin_method_symbols_2026-11-04, 0, "Recovered schema-invalid row from bug_descriptions; no execution or resolution claim; original_row_"

    llm_caret_native_entry_closure_bare_builtin_method_symbols_2026-11-04, 1, "2026-11-10 premise re-check (release/1.0.0 968e1778770, interpreter lane, Fable fix lane): the suspected mechanism -- method_calls_literals.spl emitting a Call to the bare method name when receiver.type_ is nil -- does not exist on the current tree. (1) The unresolved-method path (reject_unresolved_method_call_v1 ~L2493) is fail-closed: it emits rt_panic + const-0 (Task #145), never a bare symbol; no site in src/compiler/50.mir emits MirConstValue.Str(method). (2) Literal/primitive receivers lower without a type-inference pass to rt_string_len/rt_string_trim/rt_string_starts_with, rt_len (known array), rt_enum_payload (Err(..).unwrap_err), numeric conversion owners: new spec test/01_unit/compiler/mir/bare_builtin_method_literal_receiver_spec.spl 6/6 green (text/array/int/float/bool/Result literal, one it per family). (3) Cross-module nil-typed receivers: test/01_unit/compiler/mir/bare_builtin_method_carrier_link_probe_spec.spl 3/3 green; a probe lowering a lib struct with len/starts_with methods WITHOUT the lib module as a provider still emitted owner-qualified probe.tok.Span.len / probe.tok.Span.starts_with. Collateral spec defect found+fixed: the carrier spec's four negative probes searched for a backslash-escaped value-key spelling the MIR serializer never emits (it prints plain quotes), so they could never fail; rewritten to plain-quote probes with an rt_string_trim sanity pin, re-run 3/3 green (red-proof: the literal spec's rt_len positive probe failed 5/6 with the escaped spelling, 6/6 after). The 95-module native-build link failure was never reproduced here (no heavy builds on this lane) and the record itself says source-inspection-only; closed-obsolete. If the bare len/trim/starts_with/unwrap_err link failure recurs, re-file naming the lane (Rust seed native-build vs stage2 pure-Simple) and attach the MIR dump of the Call whose callee is the bare name."

